\b Stash \endash  clipboard manager\b0\par
\par
\b Installs for you only.\b0\line
Stash is installed into %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Programs\\Stash for the current user. It needs no administrator rights and makes no machine-wide changes.\par
\par
\b Everything stays on this machine.\b0\line
Clipboard history is kept in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Stash. Stash makes no network connections of any kind.\par
\par
\b Your history is not encrypted.\b0\line
History is stored as plain files. Anything that can already read your user profile can read your clipboard history \endash  the same exposure as the clipboard history built into Windows. Stash skips clips that applications flag as sensitive, such as copies made from a password manager, and you can exclude specific applications in Settings.\par
\par
\b Uninstalling keeps your history.\b0\line
Removing Stash deletes the program but leaves your clips in place. To remove them too, delete the %LOCALAPPDATA%\\Stash folder.\par
\par
Provided as is, without warranty of any kind.\par
